Title: "Tuple Expressions"
Id: "98559f5a-7f2e-4496-9e5d-06a553e75990"

Text: "Tuple expressions use parentheses and contain two or more elements.

```mlg-fragment
(x, y)
(a, b, c)
(x, +, y)
```

One-element tuples are not supported. Parentheses around a single expression are grouping syntax. Operators may appear as tuple elements, as in `(+, x)`.

A tuple literal satisfies a command's nominal type requirement structurally: the checker compares its component count and positional component specs against the required type."
Id: "68b4d6db-7521-4f23-8239-c8d167cbfdd9"
